e the fee-debit authorization in each advisory agreement and re-paper the c=
lient onto the firm's revised agreement, which contains no withdrawal autho=
rity; to transfer custody of those accounts to Wexbury Fiduciary Trust unde=
r agreements conferring no instruction authority on the firm; and to obtain=
 a surprise examination by an independent public accountant with the corres=
